window.FAQ_SEARCH_INDEX=[{"title": "Best Practices for Filming in the Classroom: Keep the Camera Steady", "href": "best-practices-for-filming-in-the-classroom-keep-the-camera-steady.html", "text": "Secure your camera to a tripod or mount if possible. If you don't have a mount or tripod, make sure your camera is on a steady surface or leaning against something stable. With the exception of panning and tilting to keep the subject in frame, let the camera be a quiet observer. Slow panning is also a must (movement or rotation of the camera). You can lose the viewer with a shot that is too far or wide to see what you’re talking about, or if you zoom in and the result is a shaky shot. If your video is covering something small, get up close so the viewer can see it. For larger lesson materials, zoom out so that the subject is captured completely within the video's frame."}, {"title": "Can I Add More Users?", "href": "can-i-add-more-users.html", "text": "There are two ways in which you are able to initiate in adding users to your user list: Your Client Success Manager will be able to do this for you. If you'd like to do so, please speak with your Client Success Manager for extra training for this right."}, {"title": "Can I Delete My Video Once I've Uploaded It?", "href": "can-i-delete-my-video-once-ive-uploaded-it.html", "text": "Teaching Channel puts you in control of the videos that you want to Self Reflect on, Share and Submit. If you are not satisfied with the video you have uploaded, follow the steps below. 1. Go to the Video Activities and locate your video. 2. Select the kebob button (three vertical dots) on the top right corner. 3. Click the Delete Video button from the drop-down. 4. Confirm the action within the pop-up. Note: this action is only possible before the Sharing and Submitting processes have happened."}, {"title": "Can I See All User Data for my Account?", "href": "can-i-look-at-my-accounts-entire-user-data.html", "text": "All users are able to view their own data. To get access to see all of your account's user data, speak with your Client Success Manager. Your Client Success Manager is able to provide you certain permissions to view this type of data. They can also help you gather other data, depending on your coaching needs. Some examples of data collected is: Number of logins Number of video uploads Number of feedback comments sent Number of Teaching Channel videos watched and for how long"}, {"title": "Can I Reflect on Teaching Channel Libary Videos?", "href": "can-i-reflect-on-teaching-channel-libary-videos.html", "text": "1. Select any video from the Teaching Channel Video Library 2. Click Add to... 3. Select Add to My Activities 3. If you're ready to reflect, select Go to My Activities in the upper right corner of your screen If you're not ready to reflect, dismiss the notification. You can find the video in your Video Activities later. 4. Click the drop-down arrow on the video, choose a Framework, and Save . 5. Select Reflect on Video 5. When you see an indicator present in a video you're watching and want to acknowledge it, select the indicator from the chosen Framework, type a comment in the box, and click Comment"}, {"title": "Can I Remove Users From My Account?", "href": "can-i-remove-users-from-my-account.html", "text": "There are two ways in which you can remove users from your account: Your Client Success Manager is able to remove users from your account for you. Speak with your Client Success Manager about getting extra training for this right."}, {"title": "How Do I Share a Video?", "href": "can-i-share-teaching-channel-library-videos.html", "text": "1. Find the video you would like to share in the Video Library. 2. Click Share in the lower-right corner of the video. 3. Select your recipients using the cohort dropdown menu. You can choose one or multiple users to share the video with."}, {"title": "How to Capture Great Audio", "href": "capture-great-audio.html", "text": "The microphone is on the camera. Be sure your camera is close to the source of the sound for the best audio quality. Good microphones can also be purchased at a relatively low cost. Be conscious of the noise going on in the background."}, {"title": "Help Form", "href": "contact-us-engage-platform.html", "text": "If you need to get in touch with us, please complete the form and we will respond to your inquiry within one business day."}, {"title": "How Do I Access the Video Library?", "href": "how-do-i-access-the-teaching-channel-video-library.html", "text": "There are two ways to get to the Video Library: 1. Click the magnifying glass icon at the top right of the menu to be taken to the Video Library. 2. Alternatively, you can select the waffle icon at the top right of the page and click Video Library."}, {"title": "How Do I Add a Video to a Playlist?", "href": "how-do-i-add-a-video-to-a-playlist.html", "text": "1. While viewing a video select +Add to.... 2. Select the playlist you'd like the video to be added to. Or 2.  Create a new playlist from the dropdown and add the video there. From there, when you select the playlist from the playlist page, you will see the video added."}, {"title": "How Do I Create a Playlist?", "href": "how-do-i-create-a-playlist.html", "text": "1. Find a video in the Video Library that you would like to add to your playlist. 2. Click Add To in the lower-right corner of the video, then select Add to Playlist . 3. Select Create New Playlist and enter a title and description for your playlist. 4. Add additional videos by repeating the process and selecting your newly created playlist. Please note: A playlist must contain at least three videos before it can be shared with others."}, {"title": "How Do I Edit My Profile?", "href": "how-do-i-edit-my-profile.html", "text": "1. From the Home page , click your initials in the top right corner. 2. Select View Profile. 3. Upload a profile picture and/or edit your name. You can also change your email and/or password from here too. 4. Select Save."}, {"title": "How Do I Reset My Password?", "href": "how-do-i-reset-my-password.html", "text": "1. Click on the \"Forgot Password?\" button beneath the login fields: 2. Enter the email address that your Teaching Channel account is registered under. Then click          the \"Send Reset Instructions\" button: 3. An email containing a password reset link will be sent to your registered email address. Use that link to reset your password. Please note, the password requirements are: be at least 8 characters, include at least 1 upper case letter include at least 1 lower case letter include at least 1 number include at least 1 special character from @, #, $ and/or % Once you set your new password, you can then use it to log into your account."}, {"title": "How Do I Submit a Video for Observation?", "href": "how-do-i-submit-a-video.html", "text": "How to Begin the Submission Process: To begin the submission process, you will need to go to Video Activities in the navigation. These submissions are more formal observations. They include a rating system for the observer of the video to fill out. It is important to note that you can only create a submission on the videos you have put into Video Activities. Self-reflection comments will also be viewable when the video is submitted for observation. Select the carrot on the top left corner of the video you would like to share. Click on the “ Submit Video ” button. A pop-up will appear and you will select the cohort you would like to submit to. Then, you will check the individual you would like to submit to. There is a limit to the number of people you would like to submit to. You can only submit to one person. After you click the “ Submit Video ” button, the individual you have submitted the video to will be notified via email. You are able to submit the same video multiple times. Just repeat the process above. These will be separate observations."}, {"title": "How Do I Trim My Video?", "href": "how-do-i-trim-my-video.html", "text": "Tap on the video you'd like to edit. Drag the left and right anchors in the top bar so the section of video you'd like to keep is within them. The left anchor lets you choose the start point and the right anchor lets you decide where the video clip will end. Tap the Trim button in the upper right hand corner. Tap on either Trim Original or Save as New Clip. The second option preserves the original video and creates a new file for your trimmed version."}, {"title": "How Do I Trim My Video?", "href": "how-do-i-trim-my-video-1.html", "text": "Open the Gallery app on your Android mobile device. In the Gallery, choose the video you wish to edit. From the playback screen, tap the three dots in the upper-right corner, and select “ Trim ” from the dropdown menu. Use the trim selectors on the playback timeline to adjust your video clip (The left selector lets you choose the start point and the right selector lets you decide where it will end). When you’re finished trimming your video, tap “ Save ”. The app will prepend your video filename with “ TRIM_(filename) ”. A pop-up will ask you to select a player app to view your new video. Select the app you are most comfortable with to view your shortened video clip. If you don’t want to open the video in the video player, you can simply cancel out of the operation and share your shortened video to the service or location you desire. http://www.howtogeek.com/201843/how-to-trim-and-cut-videos-on-your-android-device/ Samsung Devices Open the Gallery or Videos app on your Samsung mobile device. Select the video you wish to trim. Once the video opens, tap the three options dots in the upper-right corner then tap Edit -> Studio -> Video Trimmer . Use the yellow marker to advance the video to where you want your clip focused on. Use the selectors to pick your start and end points (The left marker lets you choose the start point and the right marker lets you decide where it will end). When you’re finished, tap “ Done ”. A popup will appear asking you name your new video. Unlike Android, Samsung doesn’t automatically save the new file, so you will have to give it a filename, and then tap “ Save ”"}, {"title": "How to Create a Discussion", "href": "how-to-create-a-discussion.html", "text": "To create a discussion, you will need to go to the Video Activities tab within the menu bar. These discussions are meant to help promote collaborative conversation about your practice. It is important to note that you can only create a discussion on the videos you have put into the Video Activities. Self-reflection comments will be viewable when the video is shared for discussion. Select the > icon on the top left corner of the video you would like to share. Click on the “ Share Video ” button. A pop-up will appear and you will select the cohort you would like to share with. Then, you will check the individuals you would like to share with. There is no limit to the number of people you would like to share with. You can share with as many people as you would like. After you click the “ Share Video ” button, the individuals you have shared the video with will be notified via email. You are able to share the same video multiple times. Just repeat the process above. These will be separate conversations."}, {"title": "How Do I Observe a Submission?", "href": "how-to-do-i-begin-the-sumbmission-process.html", "text": "The observer of the video can access the video from the Notifications section of the platform (the bell icon) by selecting the “ View Observation ” button or from within the Video Activities section. When in Video Activities, the observer will click the > button of the new video and select “ Open ”. There are 4 parts to the submission observation process: Feedback , where the observer will leave observational comments that will be annotated into the video. Rating , where the observer will rate the video based off of the embedded framework. General Feedback , where the observer can provide more elaborate feedback on the video. Recommended Resources , where the observer can provide links, documents and Account Library resources. These resources can be anything from graphic organizers, lesson plan templates, online resources or other demo videos that might help in the feedback process. Once the observer selects “ Send Feedback ”, the owner of the video will be notified via email. The owner of the video will be able to review all sections filled out by the observer. After reviewing the feedback, they will need to acknowledge the feedback on the Acknowledge Feedback page. From there, the submission cycle will be completed."}, {"title": "How Do I Save a Video?", "href": "how-to-save-videos.html", "text": "Favorites are where your saved videos will be saved. There are a couple of places where you can Favorite a video. From the Video Library page: Click the kebab button and select Add to Favorites. From the Video Page: Click the Add to... button and select Add to Favorites."}, {"title": "How Do I Search for a Video?", "href": "how-to-search-for-content.html", "text": "Within the Teaching Channel Library, there are 2,200+ carefully curated videos. There are multiple filters to help you find what you might be looking for. Begin by clicking Filter List at the top right of the Video Library. There, you will see four filter drop-downs: Grade Subject Topic Video Length As you select filters from the drop-downs, the content will filter for you. You can also search for keywords within the Search Bar. Just type into the Search Bar and hit enter on the keyboard. Be sure to use the new Standards Filter! Here you will be able to find videos aligned to Math, English Language Arts, Science and the Danielson 2022 Framework for Teaching."}, {"title": "Know What's in Your Background", "href": "know-what-is-in-your-background.html", "text": "Don’t film against a sunny window. Don’t film a distracting background."}, {"title": "Mobile Accessories Made Easy", "href": "mobile-accessories-made-easy.html", "text": "Lens adapter kits that allow you to capture better videos are available if you are using a smartphone. Mounts that allow you to attach smaller cameras or smartphones to tripods are available as well."}, {"title": "Reports", "href": "reports-dummy-article.html", "text": "There are multiple ways that data is collected for each user. This data varies depending on which features you have licensed. To begin, click Reports in the navigation: Library Reports: Usage Statistics Resource Videos Watched Activity Reports: Video Statistics Videos Shared Videos Submitted Instructional Focus Observation Data Report Please contact your Client Success Manager to discuss data reporting further."}, {"title": "Commenting on a Shared Video", "href": "the-discussion-process.html", "text": "Users can access the video from the Notifications page (bell icon) and by selecting the “ Join Discussion ” button within the notification. A user can also access the shared discussion by going to Video Activities, opening the > icon to the video and selecting the “ Open ” button in the Shared row. Once on the shared page, users can leave comments on the video. Comments can be linked with tags. Tag options are: Type , such as Clarification, Context, Kudos etc. Framework , in which comments can be aligned to standards and sub-standards from your embedded framework. Resources can also be attached to comments in the forms of Links and Files . The user will want to select the paperclip icon to open those options. Comments will be time-stamped on the timeline of the video and will populate in chronological order of the video beneath the comment box. The owner of the video will be notified via email that comments have been left on the video they shared on a 24 hours basis."}, {"title": "Thoughtful Recordings", "href": "thoughtful-recordings.html", "text": "1. Choose the right recording device. Will you be recording from your computer, tablet, or mobile device? 2. Consider what you are trying to record. What segment of the lesson are you trying to capture? Who is the focus of the video? Are you focusing on teacher actions or student actions? 3. Figure out where you will place the recording device. Place your recording device somewhere where it will capture the action in the classroom without a human supporting it. 4. Decide the length of the video ahead of time. 5. Speak clearly. 6. You will want to hear yourself and the students. Think about device placement, the volume of your voice, and your students’ voices when students speak. It might be helpful for you to repeat what they are saying. 7. Go for a test run. Before you are expected to share a video, test it out. You can then watch the video and hear the audio quality and adjust as necessary."}, {"title": "How To: Upload a Video", "href": "uploading-a-video.html", "text": "Video Uploading To upload a video into Video Activities from the Dashboard, scroll down to the Your Video Activities row and click \" Upload Video. Alternatively, click Video Activities in the navigation. Select the “ Upload Video” button on the top right corner. Click the “ Click to upload ” button and select the video file from your computer. Note: file size may not exceed 3GB and files must be MP4 or MOV format. As the video uploads, complete the following steps: Type the title of the video into the “ Title ” textbox. The title of the video is what you want to name it. Click the “Click to upload” button and select the video file from your computer. Note: file size may not exceed 3GB and files must be MP4 or MOV format. As the video uploads, complete the following steps: Type the title of the video into the “ Title ” textbox. The title of the video is what you want to name it. Describe the video within the “ Video Description ” textbox. This will help provide overall context about the video. Select the grade level associated with the video from the “ Grade Level ” dropdown. Select the subject associated with the video from the “ Subject ” dropdown. Type the session into the “ Session ” textbox. A session will help differentiate between AM or PM sessions, block scheduling or write NA, if not applicable. Type or click the number of participants in the video within the “ No. of Participants ” textbox. When the video has completed uploading, the “ Continue ” button will become clickable. Click on the “ Continue ” button. To add a link, select the “ Add Link ” button. Make sure to copy/paste or type in the entire web address into the “ URL ” textbox. Type the display name of the link into the “ Link Title to Display ” textbox. Click on the “ Add to Documentation ” button. Links can be anything from lesson plans, behavior plans, student samples and/or copies of graphic organizers stored on Google Drive or any other website. These can help provide an extra layer of context to the video. To add a file, select the “ Upload File ” button. Click the “ Click to upload ” button to open your finder. Select your file. Click on the “ Add to Documentation ” button. Similar to links, files can be anything from lesson plans, behavior plans, student samples and/or copies of graphic organizers stored on your computer. Click the “ Add to Activities ” button. It is important to note that your video will not be saved in Video Activities until you click Add to Activities at the end of the workflow."}, {"title": "What Can I Upload into the [Account] Library?", "href": "what-can-i-upload-into-the-account-library.html", "text": "The [Account] Library is a library for you to store instructional, professional and administrative resources for yourself and/or others to see. Demo video lessons, graphic organizers, behavior charts, online learning links and other resources are all able to be uploaded here. Think of this as a large folder that you can keep all your resources together."}, {"title": "Who Can See My Videos?", "href": "who-can-see-my-videos.html", "text": "None of your video uploads can be seen by other users without your permission. In order for another user to view your video uploads, you will need to share with them and/or submit your video to them. You are also able to upload your videos into the Account Library. When doing so, you will be able to select specific viewing rights that will impact who is able to see your video."}, {"title": "How Do I Share a Playlist with Everyone in the Account?", "href": "how-do-i-share-a-playlist-with-everyone.html", "text": "1. Navigate to Playlists from the homepage or the waffle menu. 2. Select the playlist you want to share. 3. Click Share . 4. From the Select Cohort dropdown, choose the cohort representing your entire school or district. This is typically labeled with your institution’s name followed by ALL . 5. Check the Select Whole Cohort box to include everyone in the cohort. 6. Click Share Playlist to complete the process. Please note: A playlist must contain at least three videos before it can be shared with others."}, {"title": "What’s the Difference Between Reflect, Share, and Submit?", "href": "reflect-share-submit.html", "text": "The platform offers three different Video Activities workflows. Use the descriptions below to determine which workflow best fits your needs, whether you’re uploading your own video or using a video from our library. 1. Reflect on a Video: Choose this option when you want to capture personal reflections and leave comments that only you can see. 2. Share a Video: Choose this option when you want to share a video with one or more people, such as your PLC cohort, an instructional coach, or a mentor teacher. This workflow allows participants to leave comments and reply to one another, creating opportunities for collaboration and shared learning. 3. Submit: Choose this option for a more formal coaching process. This workflow allows you to provide additional context and details about your uploaded video, generates reports, and supports more intentional tracking of professional growth over time."}, {"title": "How Do I Access Learning Center Courses?", "href": "how-do-i-access-learning-center-courses.html", "text": "If your organization subscribes to Teaching Channel, you can access eligible professional development courses through the Learning Center. After you receive your Teaching Channel Video Library welcome email and set up your password, follow these steps. Locate your courses 1. Log in to Teaching Channel and open the waffle menu in the top-right corner. 2. Select Learning Center , then choose My Active Courses . It may take one to two minutes for your courses to load. Select courses and complete registration 1. Next to the Bundle Placeholder, click Finalize Enrollment . 2. Use the Course Category menu or search bar to find a course, open the category, and click Select Course . Some subscriptions have predetermined courses. 3. After selecting your courses, click Register . 4. When the registration confirmation appears, click Back to My Platform Learning Center Courses . Please note: Eligible courses are included in your organization’s subscription at no additional cost. Standard pricing shown in course descriptions may not apply to your district’s included courses. Access your course 1. Click View Options and select Access Course . 2. You will be taken to your course dashboard in Canvas. Select your course to begin learning. You can return to your courses by selecting My Platform Learning Center Courses under your name in the top-right corner. How to Access Learning Center Courses — illustrated guide"}, {"title": "How Can I Track Professional Learning and Course Completion?", "href": "track-professional-learning-and-course-completion.html", "text": "For educators 1. Log in to the Teaching Channel platform. 2. Click Learning Center , then click My Course History . 3. My Course History provides information on both completed courses and current courses. 4. Access completion documentation under the View Options button next to the completed course. Download or email the completion letter for your records. For administrators Reporting features may vary depending on your organization’s subscription and assigned platform role. 1. Open Learning Center in the Teaching Channel platform. 2. Click View Student Progress to open the Administrative Teaching Channel Dashboard. 3. In the Admin Dashboard, click Student Progress . From here, you can view staff progress, filter by Not completed, In Progress, and Completed, search by user name, and export progress data to Excel. Steps on accessing the Admin Dashboard If you encounter issues, contact your designated Client Success Manager for support."}];